                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.61331/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-13T21:00:00-04:00">September 13, 1939—9
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>949. Your 1620, September 13, 1 p.m. Please convey to Stanley that abrupt
                    curtailment of British purchases of American tobacco has had distinctly adverse
                    repercussions on the American industry. Please add, however, that while the
                    action taken by the British Government is naturally disappointing to us, this
                    Government recognizes the immediate difficulties confronting the United Kingdom.
                    If you deem it appropriate, will you express the earnest hope that there will be
                    at least a partial resumption of tobacco purchases from the United States.
                    Report by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
